  "price_note": "Purchase prices and capacities are INDICATIVE foodservice wholesale figures in USD, not transcribed from the v6 workbook — its `6.Packaging` sheet carries no cost column. They exist so a kitchen can cost a recipe on day one instead of meeting a technical sheet that refuses to total. Every one of them is meant to be replaced with what this kitchen actually pays, in the packaging library. `purchase_price_amount` is per `purchase_unit_code`; a recipe consuming one piece divides it by `items_per_unit`. `capacity_quantity` is how much product one item holds, in the recipe’s own unit (kg) rather than the container’s nominal volume — a 300 cc bottle holds 0.3 kg of sauce, and same-unit arithmetic cannot be silently wrong the way a missing density can."
}
